Write a polished meeting summary email for this meeting.

Meeting: {{ $json.meetingTitle }}
Date: {{ $json.meetingDate }}
Duration: {{ $json.durationMin }} minutes
Participants: {{ $json.participants }}

Key topics covered: {{ $json.keyTopicsList }}

Action items: {{ $json.actionItemsFormatted }}

Client mood summary: {{ $json.clientMood }}

Positive responses: {{ $json.positivesList }}

Concerns raised: {{ $json.concernsList }}

Next meeting needed: {{ $json.nextMeetingNeeded }}

Write a professional meeting summary email. Plain text only. No markdown. No bullet points. Write in full paragraphs.

Structure:

Opening paragraph: Brief warm thank-you and one sentence on what was accomplished.

Key discussion points: 2 to 3 paragraphs covering the main topics in natural language. Reference what was agreed.

Action items section: List all action items with owners and deadlines in a clear numbered format.

Closing: One sentence on next steps. If next meeting is needed, say so. Sign off professionally with {{ $json.senderName }} and {{ $json.teamName }}.

